Based on the search results, "Design" is not a standard, current trim level for the most recent BMW 3 Series (G20). BMW uses "Lines" (like Sport Line, Luxury Line, Modern Line - though Modern Line was dropped in F30 facelift) or packages (like M Sport Package) to influence the design and equipment. The G20 LCI (facelifted) models use "Baseline/Sport", "M Sport", and "M Sport Pro" trims [2].

Since "Design" is not a clearly defined trim for the most recent model, providing a specific, data-backed evaluation for this exact configuration is not possible without making assumptions or extrapolations, which is against the instructions.

However, the instructions require returning ONLY JSON and defaulting to 0.00 if data is ambiguous or unclear. Given the ambiguity of the trim itself, I will interpret this as defaulting all scores to 0.00, as specific data for a "Design" trim on the most recent 3 Series is unclear or non-existent in standard documentation. This is the only way to comply with the strict output format and the instruction to default when data is unclear, even though it results in a non-informative evaluation.

